<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47904" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρρος</span></b> , 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέρσος</span></b>  (q.v.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρασύς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>courage</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				6.126
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. τινός</span>
			<i>courage to do</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				48
			</span></i>: c. gen., <i>courage against . . </i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					647b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τοὺς πολεμίους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					4.2.15
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἴσχε</span> take <i>courage!</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				807
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἔχειν περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					412
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρεσὶ θ. ἀέξειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					96
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴρειν πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					1598
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαβεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					28.15
				</span></i>
			; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἔλαβέ τινας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.92
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐμπνέειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.381
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνὶ φρεσὶ θεῖναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.76
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ δ᾽ ἐνὶ θυμῷ θῆκε . .
			θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				1.321
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν κραδίῃ βάλλειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.547
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρασχεῖν, ἐμποιεῖν τινι</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.68
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.5.17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐγγίγνεται, ἐμπίπτει
			τινί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.2.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HG</u>
				7.1.31
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμφύσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					5.2.32
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτ᾽ ἐλπίδος γὰρ οὔτε του δόξης
					ὁρῶ θ. παρ᾽ ἡμῖν ὡς . . </span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					371
				</span></i>
			: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόβοι καὶ θάρρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1107a33
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				360b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>that which gives courage</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλολυγμόν . . , θάρσος φίλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					270
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				184
			</span></i>: pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρση</span>
			<i>grounds of confidence</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1281
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			rarely in bad sense, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θράσος</span>
			, <i>audacity</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος ἄητον ἔχουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.395
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυίης θάρσος ἐνὶ στήθεσσιν
				ἐνῆκεν</span> the <i>reckless persistence</i> of a fly,
				<i><span class="en">
				17.570
			</span></i>.—On the diff. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάρσος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θράσος</span>, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θράσος</span>
			.</div>
